Chromium 156.0.8078.73 + the later changes of its release branch, for the
156.0.8078.73 tarball.

The 156 branch has gained fixes since 156.0.8078.73 (a use-after-free in
MediaStream tracks; pointer events, error events, named items, highlights,
the quota database and storage directories; V8's cppgc write barrier and
TurboShaft's stack frame size), some of them likely security fixes that
later release notes will credit.

Generated from the upstream diffs chromium/src
refs/tags/156.0.8078.73..5185e9cb62c9a95b6a881075e8baa70d54d3d29b
(refs/branch-heads/8078 on 2026-10-27) and v8 (the only dependency whose
DEPS revision changed), as served by Gitiles, with
scripts/chromium-delta/filter.py --branch-fixes: left out are files not in
the release tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and
docs, PGO/AFDO/orderfile pointers, ChromeOS LKGM, submodule pointer updates.
chrome/VERSION, DEPS and the generated LASTCHANGE files stay at
156.0.8078.73.

Commits contributing to it (oldest first; "Roll commits from side projects"
are the v8 updates: "[cppgc] Update the Steele-style barrier to always
retrace" and "[turboshaft] Bound JS stack frame size to 4KB"):
  6442ebe52d91 [M156] [MediaStream] Fix UAF in MediaStream(Audio|Video)Track::StopAndNotify
  1557ab9e6afc [M156] [MenuSimplification] Prevent duplicate Reading Mode context menu entries
  398e6b2b2e2f [M156] [MenuSimplification] Restore Partial Translate guards in simplified context menus
  23dd0d13e63b [M156] [highlights] Keep hit-test range pointers stable
  f795cb525d53 [M156] Don't hold references to name or id across UpdateName()/UpdateId()
  b61cb425758f Roll commits from side projects in M156
  27504b75fab9 [OTP] Enforce field-level and form-level OTP eligibility checks (base)
  9d98906b7519 [M156] Avoid CopyDirectory fallback in StorageDirectory::DoomPath
  439f2a316156 [M156] Defer entry removal until database scan iterator is destroyed
  e2075db3e7a4 [M156] [Quota] Remove obsolete QuotaDatabase::MoveLegacyDatabase()
  8b30ccddb585 [M156] Do not paint focus ring for display-locked <area> elements
  b40346fc7495 Roll commits from side projects in M156
  93f574f14f95 [M156] Don't send a cross-origin relatedTarget on a PointerEvent boundary event, and add more general defense-in-depth for relatedTarget.
  d473602c676c [M156] Avoid re-entry when draining pending error events

